  "question": {
    "text": "A charge $q$ is placed at one corner of a cube. The electric flux through any of the three faces adjacent to the charge is zero. The flux through any one of the other three faces is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vIn5O",
      "text": "$q / 3 \\varepsilon_{0}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2HiBA",
      "text": "$q / 6 \\varepsilon_{0}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nxkX2",
      "text": "$q / 12 \\varepsilon_{0}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a6FtQ",
      "text": "$q / 24 \\varepsilon_{0}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider the diagram\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2015_phy_a34.png\">\r\n\r\nIn above the flux coverage of three face is shown in figure. Which is like a quadrant in any plane. So, flux will be\r\n$$\r\n\\phi=\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{q}{6 \\varepsilon_{0}}=\\frac{q}{24 \\varepsilon_{0}}\r\n$$",
